@host = http://localhost:5000

### List the runtime catalog of document types
GET {{host}}/document-types

### List the compiled actor types this app hosts (one interpreted actor runs them all)
GET {{host}}/hosted-types

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Happy path: a small expense report auto-approves and settles to Archived.
# Each scenario starts by onboarding its document, which both cleans up any
# state left by a previous run and sets up the fresh definition, so the whole
# file is safe to run top-to-bottom repeatedly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Onboard an expense report: clears any prior run and deploys the ExpenseReport definition
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-001/onboard?type=ExpenseReport

### Submit it (small amount: clears the auto-approval limit)
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-001/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "alice", "amount": 250.00, "parties": ["finance", "alice"], "simulateChargeFailure": false }

### Begin review
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-001/begin-review

### Approve -think> enters Approved -> StartSettlement schedules the settlement workflow.
# The workflow notifies parties, charges, then drives the document to Archived.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Escalation + compensation: a large expense whose charge fails is compensated,
# and the workflow drives the document to SettlementFailed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-001/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approver": "bob", "note": "looks good" }

### Onboard a second expense report: clears any prior run and deploys a fresh ExpenseReport
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-002/onboard?type=ExpenseReport

### Submit a large amount that will fail the charge (exceeds the auto-approval limit)
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-002/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "carol", "amount": 8500.00, "parties": ["finance", "carol", "vendor"], "simulateChargeFailure": true }

### Begin review
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-002/begin-review

### Approve -> large amount escalates to a manager (state becomes Escalated)
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-002/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approver": "bob", "note": "over limit" }

### Manager approves -> Approved -> settlement workflow runs, charge fails, compensation runs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A different document type (Contract) is the same compiled actor, different data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/documents/exp-002/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approver": "manager", "note": "approved with budget" }

### Onboard a contract: clears any prior run and deploys the Contract definition (adds a LegalReview stage)
POST {{host}}/documents/con-001/onboard?type=Contract

### Submit
POST {{host}}/documents/con-001/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "dave", "amount": 500.00, "parties": ["legal", "dave"], "simulateChargeFailure": false }

### Begin legal review
POST {{host}}/documents/con-001/begin-legal-review

### Complete legal review -> InReview
POST {{host}}/documents/con-001/complete-legal-review

### Approve -> Approved -> settlement -> Archived
POST {{host}}/documents/con-001/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approver": "legal-lead", "note": "signed" }
